      "title": "Parametrizing an Elliptic Cylinder"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "28d23a5e-bc2a-5eb9-bf02-3fcdcac273d5",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t,y)=⟨5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t,y)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{x^{2}}{25}+\\frac{z^{2}}{16}=1.$ What is the third component of $\\mathbf{f}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall that the ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{25}+\\frac{z^{2}}{16}=1$ in the $xz$-plane has the parametrization\n\n$$\n⟨x,z⟩=⟨5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,\\quad t\\in[0,2\\pi),\n$$\n\nsince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{z^2}{16}&=\\frac{(5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2}{25}+\\frac{(4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2}{16}\\\\&=\\cos^2 t+\\sin^2 t\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t,y)=⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,y,\\,4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and $y\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nTherefore, the third component of $\\mathbf{f}$ is $4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "38ad1892-444a-52c3-9342-9be5e8505355",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "325424be-7ef3-5605-ad5f-545b8a7648fb",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "16 y^{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e83c939b-c112-5d87-b92f-420ed9ec7d9f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "23c1229f-af78-59a6-8749-8b3cb634c73e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "68c4fb5e-9cbe-5640-9c70-b84ea28403eb",
